---
/**
 * The one interactive thing on this site, and the only reason the React
 * integration is loaded at all.
 *
 * Wrapping an island is a real cost — the framework runtime, a hydration step, a
 * chunk — so it is opted into per page rather than mounted globally. A page
 * without `<Demo />` ships no framework runtime, and `test/browser.ts` measures
 * that rather than asserting it.
 *
 * `client:load` rather than `client:visible` or `client:idle`: the point of this
 * island is that it runs *immediately* on arrival, because a reader deciding
 * whether this library is worth adopting should not have to scroll to find out
 * whether it works.
 *
 * The styles live in `src/styles/ax.css` rather than in a `<style>` element here,
 * because an `.astro` file cannot hold a template literal in one.
 */

import TryIt from "./TryIt";
---

<TryIt client:load />